holiday season is being dampened by the  coronavirus pandemic again this year  especially if you're planning to travel  by air more than 700 u.s flights are  already canceled today and that's on top  of hundreds that were called off on  christmas eve airlines say they're being  hit with staff shortages due to the  rapidly spreading omicron variant the  first known case of omicron in the u.s  was reported on december 1st the variant  is now the dominant strain of the  coronavirus accounting for about 73  percent of all cases in this country and  it spread quickly the average number of  new cases is up 45 percent in the past  week and it's more than double what it  was on december first the good news for  now is that despite the surge in cases  new hospitalizations have stayed mostly  flat nationwide but the holiday travel  woes are the latest reminder of just how  disruptive the pandemic has become  at airports across the country flight  cancellations were mostly due to airline  staff calling out sick or reporting  they'd been exposed to the virus there's  just so much that  any employer can do  for those that work in offices employers  can say stay home and work remotely  but that's not the case with airline  personnel earlier this week delta asked  the cdc to shorten isolation times for  vaccinated airline workers who test  positive from 10 days to 5. at the same  time air travel was projected to spike  184 percent this year over 2020 with 30  million passing through tsa checkpoints  now that it's been more than a year  since vaccinations became available  we're at much lower risk this christmas  than we were last christmas but we still  must hang our stockings with care dr  william shafer is an infectious disease  specialist offering advice for the  holidays  and i hope we're all gathering  vaccinated and boosted  and then in addition before we all  gather many of us are getting a rapid  test on christmas day to make sure that  we're all negative then we can  share the joy  in a much more relaxed fashion but with  so many not able to take off there was  more frustration than relaxing the  machine's not working right  it's just terrible it's awful it's awful  nice siblings and my parents i think  they're a little bit stressed out right  now trying to figure it out even as many  prepared to travel by getting tested i  think if they've been tested before  they've gotten on the plane  then i think you're in really pretty  good shape but as predicted omicron  spreads fast new york reported nearly 45  000 new cases friday a 14 jump from the  day before breaking records for the  seventh time in just over a week in los  angeles the number of daily cases  tripled in three days to nearly ten  thousand in many places testing is free  but what about holiday get-togethers for  people who aren't tested let's all  gather together wear the mask  keep social distancing except during the  time when we're eating and religious  services in many places are taking extra  precautions with more churches offering  online services this year we are having  the masks available and we are  distancing so that we can make sure that  christmas is not only merry but is safe
 

